From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gehrig Wilcox <lougehrig10@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:25:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Decide autotune config set at launch time, not import
 time

autotune_configs() is evaluated when a kernel is decorated, i.e. at import.
torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True) (or set_deterministic_mode) called
after `import mamba_ssm` therefore left full autotuning on, and the chosen
configs - which change reduction order - could differ between processes.

Replace @triton.autotune(configs=autotune_configs([...])) with
@autotune(configs=[...]): a thin wrapper holding a fully-autotuned kernel and
a lazily-built deterministic one (deterministic_configs(): cached autotuning
with TRITON_CACHE_AUTOTUNING=1, the TRITON_AUTOTUNE_BLOCK_SIZE_* filter, or
the cheapest config). use_deterministic_mode() is checked on every launch.
.configs returns the full list (workspace sizing stays valid in both modes);
.best_config returns the config of the most recent launch.

Applies to every autotuned kernel in mamba_ssm, including the Mamba3 and
Mamba3-MIMO Triton kernels, which previously had no deterministic configs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
